Helios DXVK fork: D3D11.1 target-independent rasterization on mixed samples

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0016 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

Direct2D fills complex geometry (the Windows 11 shell's vector icons) with
target-independent rasterization: ForcedSampleCount 16 in a rasterizer state
made with CreateRasterizerState1, a single-sample render target, and a pixel
shader that derives its alpha from the covered samples in SV_Coverage. DXVK
dropped ForcedSampleCount from D3D11_RASTERIZER_DESC1 (only the DESC2 path
kept it) and took the rasterization sample count from the render targets
whenever one was bound, so those draws rasterized at one sample and every
covered pixel got 1/16 of its coverage (guest/windows/tools/d2d_tir_probe.cpp:
maximum alpha 16 instead of 255).

- D3D11RasterizerState::PromoteDesc(D3D11_RASTERIZER_DESC1) keeps
  ForcedSampleCount, as the DESC2 path does.
- With VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples (NVK on Maxwell B+), the rasterizer
  state's sample count is used when it is above the render targets' count
  and neither a depth-stencil target nor sample rate shading is in use
  (Vulkan does not allow mixed samples with either; D3D leaves both
  undefined under TIR). DxvkGraphicsPipelineStateInfo::rasterizationSamples()
  decides for the pipeline's multisample state, the dynamic rasterization
  samples and the sample locations alike. Such pipelines chain
  VkAttachmentSampleCountInfoAMD with the render targets' sample count
  (dynamic rendering assumes the rasterization sample count otherwise),
  which is part of the fragment output state's key.
- The D3D11 rasterizer sample count spec constant (sampleinfo / samplepos on
  the rasterizer) follows.

Without the extension, or with sample counts that match, the rasterization
sample count is what it was.

